# This directory is linked to ~/.config/herdr, so herdr writes its runtime
# state here alongside the config: sockets, logs, session.json, lock files.
#
# This repo is public, so the rule is deny-by-default: ignore everything and
# opt individual files back in. That way a future herdr release writing new
# state here cannot leak it by accident.
*
!.gitignore
!config.toml
